IMPORT prelude

§ `A domain module, imported by its neighbour`

-- The other half of `imports.l4`. Nothing here is `@export`ed and nothing here
-- is compiled on its own: `l4 catala imported-domain.l4` refuses it for having
-- no exported decision, which is correct. It exists so that `imports.l4` has
-- something to import, and so that the three things an importer can reach —
-- a record, an enumeration, and a plain helper function — each have a witness.
--
-- House style for this corpus (see `miles-card-domain.l4`, the real subject
-- this pair was cut down from): one module owns the nouns, and every module
-- that answers a question over them imports these types rather than
-- redeclaring its own.

DECLARE Band IS ONE OF
    Lower
    Upper

-- A record whose own field type is the enumeration above, so that importing
-- `Assessment` has to drag `Band` in behind it.
DECLARE Assessment
    HAS `taxable amount` IS A NUMBER
        band             IS A Band

-- An ordinary helper. It is not `@export`ed, so under R1 it compiles to a
-- private Catala toplevel `declaration … depends on … equals` — in the
-- IMPORTER's emitted module, because everything lands in one `.catala_en`.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`band for` n MEANS IF n GREATER THAN 1000 THEN Upper ELSE Lower
